The x86_64 part of musl's commit 27b485a2 ("math: fix expl on x86", 2026-08-26, after the 1.2.5 release), backported
unchanged: the shortcut that returns 2^trunc(x) starts at |x| >= 2^15 instead of 2^14, since for x <= -16384 that
power of two does not underflow to zero. libc-test's math/expl checks it (plan step S7.2).

